    rcap:coreSentence40 "The criteria for discontinuation specific to each domain are specified in the relevant DSA." ;
    rcap:evidenceDoc "Endothelial Modulation Domain-Specific Appendix 2" ;
    rcap:evidenceSection "8.3.6" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "The following reasons should prompt discontinuation of imatinib therapy: • If a patient develops neutropenia (neutrophil count <1.0 x 109 /L) and/or thrombocytopenia (platelet count <50 x 109 /L), stop imatinib and do not restart • If a patient develops elevation in bilirubin 3 times the upper limit of normal or ALT/AST 5 times the upper limit of normal, imatinib should be discontinued and not restarted • If a patient develops a severe adverse reaction, imatinib should be discontinued and not restarted The study interventions can be discontinued at any time by the treating clinician if doing so is regarded as being in the best interests of the patient." ;
    rcap:readingOf rcap:DomainDesign_END ;
    rcap:response "fills" ;
    rcap:responseSection "8.3.6" ;
    rcap:responseStatement rcap:c2fd0baa5ef,
        rcap:ce5d9618bb0 ;
    rcap:reviewStatus "analyst-reading; map, rules and responses approved 2026-10-25" ;
    rcap:role "paired" ;
    rcap:rule "D-content" ;
    rcap:sameText40 "True" ;
    rcap:secondaryResponse "defers_back" ;
    rcap:topic "discontinuation criteria" .

