rcap:delegation-9c192163e1 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        rcap:DelegationReading ;
    rcap:allocationKind "delegation" ;
    rcap:coreSentence40 "Whether or not an intervention is regarded as having an established safety profile, and any additional reporting requirements, will be specified in the relevant DSA." ;
    rcap:evidenceDoc "COVID-19 Immunoglobulin Therapy Domain-Specific Appendix 4" ;
    rcap:evidenceSection "11.2" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "Other SAEs should be reported only where, in the opinion of the site investigator, the event might reasonably have occurred as a consequence of a study intervention or study participation (see relevant core protocol documents).",
        "The occurrence of the following should be screened for and reported as SAEs for all patients in this domain, irrespective of intervention allocation: • Severe allergic reaction or anaphylaxis • Transfusion-associated Acute Lung Injury (TRALI) • Transfusion-associated Circulatory Overload (TACO) • Transfusion-associated Dyspnea (TAD) • Acute serious hemolytic reaction, defined a fever and other symptoms/signs or hemolysis within 24 hours of transfusion, confirmed by a fall in hemoglobin AND one or more of the following: o Rise in lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) o Rise in bilirubin o Positive direct antiglobulin test (DAT) o Positive crossmatch These are reactions that are based on the definitions used and reported to the local, regional or national hemovigilance system at each participating site." ;
    rcap:readingOf rcap:DomainDesign_IG ;
    rcap:response "fills_by_reference" ;
    rcap:responseSection "11.2" ;
    rcap:reviewStatus "analyst-reading; map, rules and responses approved 2026-10-25" ;
    rcap:role "paired" ;
    rcap:rule "D-backref" ;
    rcap:sameText40 "True" ;
    rcap:topic "established safety profile and reporting" .

rcap:delegation-9d0c36ce34 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        rcap:DelegationReading ;
    rcap:allocationKind "delegation" ;
    rcap:coreSentence40 "Any alternative gamma that will be set, and hence the unit-of-analysis, for each domain-Strata pair will be specified in each DSA." ;
    rcap:evidenceDoc "COVID-19 Immunoglobulin Therapy Domain-Specific Appendix 4" ;
    rcap:evidenceSection "10.2" ;
    rcap:evidenceText "Administration of a monoclonal antibody directed against SARS-CoV-2 was an exclusion criteria in all earlier versions of this DSA.",
        "All patients recruited using versions of this DSA prior to Version 3 are classified as members of the No Prior Monoclonal Antibody sub-group.",
        "Borrowing is permitted between States, i.e.",
        "So as to achieve continuity with the initial phase of this domain, a stratum is defined as comprising patients who are immune suppressed.",
        "The population of interest that will be reported as a result of the amendment of this domain are patients who have received an allocation in the Immunoglobulin Domain, including patients who have already been recruited and treated with convalescent plasma, as specified in earlier versions of this DSA.",
        "The unit-of-analysis for this domain consists of all patients who have received an allocation in this domain, and is further stratified by illness severity state at time of enrollment (defined as either Moderate State or Severe State) and Immune Suppressed Strata.",
        "This stratum definition will be applied retrospectively to patients enrolled using earlier versions of this domain and applied prospectively, operationalized as eligibility criteria, for Version 3 of this DSA onwards (i.e., only patients meeting this stratum definition are recruited using this version of the DSA).",
        "borrowing will occur between Moderate and Severe states." ;
    rcap:readingOf rcap:DomainDesign_IG ;
